d  folio that is specifically designed for  this model and what makes it really  unique is that compared to the magic  keyboard case for the iPad Pro or the  iPad Air like I have right here you can  actually detach the keyboard section on  the bottom while keeping the back of it  intact and use it as a stand just like  you can see on Apple's website this is  awesome especially since it has the  function function keys which the  original magic keyboard for the more  expensive iPad Pro does not have and  speaking of the M2 iPad Pro this is  basically the most disappointing update  ever because there's only a couple of  changes you get the M2 Chip instead of  the M1 you get Bluetooth 5.3 which is  nice and Wi-Fi 6E which is also nice but  other than that there's really no other  major changes yes you can record with  prores but who's going to be recording  with an iPad and finally the new M2 iPad  Pro supports the new hover apple pencil  which seems more like a software feature  to me because it's been available on  Samsung tablets since 2012. but anyway  those were the new iPads and now let's  get into the actual prices of the entire  six iPad lineup first of all you have  the previous generation iPad 9 which you  can now get on sale for 300 which is  honestly a really good deal because the  new iPad had 10 starts at 450 dollars  with the same 64 gigs of storage then of  course we have the iPad Mini 6 which is  on sale for 459 dollars basically 10  bucks more than the iPad 10 and the  benefit with this guy compared to that  is that you get a laminated display with  P3 colors which is really nice you have  the support for the apple pencil second  generation with no weirdness with that  whole adapter that you need and you have  the a15 bionic chip as well as the very  nice portable design but of course this  cannot support a full keyboard like the  new magic keyboard folio which gives  some points to the iPad 10. and now of  course you also have the iPad Air 5  which is usually 600 but it's now on  sale for 519 which is actually a pretty  good deal and by the way all these  Amazon deals I'll give links to down in  the description below so definitely  check those out now however I would not  recommend this new iPad Air 5 because  there are only a couple of differences  that might not be that big of a deal to  you guys as you can see right here I  have the iPad Air in the middle and the  iPad 10 on the right they both have 10.9  inch displays the air has the M1 chip  which is a lot more performance while  the iPad has the A14 which by the way  I'm gonna get into because it's not the  full story of course they both have the  12 megapixel cameras on the front with  the iPad 10 finally having a landscape  camera which is actually a big win they  both have USBC support for 5G and the  iPad Air has the benefit of having the  P3 wide color gamut with the  anti-reflective coating and fully  laminated display but honestly other  than that there's not that many  advantages with the iPad Air yes you do  have apple pencil 2nd gen support but  not much else and even the bluetooth  specs are better on the new iPad 10 you  have Bluetooth tooth 5.2 so with that  said I'd honestly recommend going with  the iPad 10 over the new iPad Air 5.  however things change when you look at  the iPad Air 4 that was back in 2020 and  it is very similar to the new iPad Air 5  with only a few changes of course it has  the same A14 chip as the new iPad 10  however it's actually going to be faster  in terms of graphics performance because  Apple mentioned in their Newsroom  article that the A14 chip and the iPad  10 is only 10 faster than the previous  iPad 9 in terms of GPU performance which  actually means it's going to be very  slow around 7 700 GPU score in metal  geekbench 5 compared to over 12  000 with the iPad Airs version of the  A14 so you're going to get better  performance with this guy right here  which by the way a renewed on Amazon  only 430 bucks even cheaper than the new  iPad 10. this is the one I would go with  if you're considering the iPad 10 to be  completely honest and then finally we  have the new M2 iPad Pros both in the 11  inch and 12.9 inch sizes now the M2 is  actually a decent deal eight hundred  dollars and you're getting the promotion  120 hertz display you're getting the  extra camera system on the back with  lidar you're getting Thunderbolt  connectivity you're getting Bluetooth  5.3 and Wi-Fi 6E there are some good  advantages with the main one being the  pro motion display that's the main  reason I would go with the new iPad Pro  however you can still find a renewed M1  iPad Pro the previous model for 650  dollars renewed on Amazon that is  actually a killer deal only 200 bucks  more than the new iPad 10. this might be  the one what people want to go with if  they want a really nice high-end iPad  best bang for the buck without spending  way too much money this is a really  really good deal but now with all that  said let me give you guys a quick  buyer's guide rundown of all of these  iPads and which ones I recommend for  each use case if you're just looking for  the cheapest new and fresh iPad you can  get I would honestly recommend still the  iPad and 9th gen for only 300 bucks on  Amazon that's still a very good deal now  if you want something for your kids  that's still portable fresh powerful  really this iPad Mini 6 is great it's  perfect for gaming for kids everything  the modern design USBC it's got  everything built in I really like this  for only around 450 bucks the same price  as the iPad 10. so if you can spend at  least 450 I'd probably go with this one  now if you want a larger display like a  10.9 inch and you want to use that new  magic keyboard folio to kind of use it  as a laptop replacement then honestly  the iPad 10 is still a great deal but on  the other hand you can just get the  renewed iPad Air 4. at this point I do  not recommend the iPad Air M1 the fifth  generation I don't think it's a good  price even on sale don't get it either  get one of the other ones or go up to  the iPad Pro and with that said speaking  of the iPad Pro I probably would not get  the M2 version unless you really care  about the extra performance maybe you  really love that hover apple pencil  feature that you really want or you care  a lot about Wi-Fi 6E and Bluetooth 5.3  then maybe you should get the new M2  iPad Pro but while you can you could  just get the M1 models so with that said  hopefully this video got rid of some of  that confusion and helps you decide  which iPad you should buy definitely  check out the links to all those great  sales down below and let me know what  you think in the comment section click  the circle above to subscribe for more  videos like this one and we'll see you  in the next video  [Music]
 

